}
```

---

# 12. Order Timeline

Create a structured timeline.

Instead of

```json
history: [...]
```

Return

```json
timeline: [
    {
        title: "Order Submitted",
        description: "Customer submitted the order.",
        time: "18 Jul 2026 • 10:30 AM"
    },
    {
        title: "Quotation Sent",
        description: "Quotation has been sent to the customer.",
        time: "18 Jul 2026 • 11:12 AM"
    }
]
```

---

# 13. Order Summary

Every order should include

```json
summary: {
    totalItems: 5,
    totalQuantity: 320,
    estimatedCompletion: "22 Jul 2026",
    paymentStatus: "Paid",
    deliveryMethod: "Pickup"
}
```

---

# 14. Populate Relationships

Review every Order endpoint and ensure relationships are populated.

Examples include

* customer
* branch
* service
* category
* quotation
* payment
* assigned staff

Avoid N+1 query issues by using efficient population, joins, or aggregation where appropriate.

---

# 15. Remove Backend-Only Fields

Do not expose

* __v
* password
* refreshToken
* deletedAt
* internalNotes
* audit metadata
* internal database IDs unless explicitly required

---

# 16. Standardize API Responses

Order responses should be clean and consistent.

Example

```json
{
    "orderNumber": "PD-2026-00124",

    "customer": {
        "fullName": "Kwame Mensah",
        "phone": "+233..."
    },

    "branch": {
        "name": "Print Hub East Legon"
    },

    "service": {
        "name": "Banner Printing"
    },

    "status": {
        "code": "PRINTING",
        "label": "In Production",
        "color": "info"
    },

    "payment": {
        "status": "Paid",
        "amount": 350,
        "currency": "GHS"
    },

    "createdAtFormatted": "18 Jul 2026",

    "summary": {
        "totalItems": 3,
        "estimatedCompletion": "22 Jul 2026"
    }
}
```

---

# 17. Apply Everywhere

Search the backend for every endpoint related to:

* Order list
* Order details
* Customer orders
* Branch orders
* Admin orders
* Dashboard statistics
* Recent orders
* Search endpoints
* Export endpoints

Ensure they all return consistent, human-readable data.

---

# Deliverables

1. Refactor all order-related serializers, DTOs, transformers, aggregation pipelines, and controllers to return human-readable responses.
2. Populate related entities instead of exposing raw IDs.
3. Standardize response formats across all order endpoints.
4. Preserve internal IDs only where required for backend logic, never as the primary display value.
5. Ensure the frontend can render order tables and detail pages without additional lookup requests.
6. Maintain backward compatibility where practical by introducing formatted fields rather than breaking existing API contracts, unless a breaking change is explicitly justified and documented.
7. Produce a summary listing every modified endpoint, every response field improved, and any recommended follow-up refactors.
